Q: Is it possible to create a git bundle of a revision range with minimal prerequisites that can be applied to a shallow clone? A: <p>After a bunch of experimentation, I was able to cobble together a hacky approach that seems to produce a thick pack:</p>
<ol>
<li>Disable delta compression temporarily: <code>git config set core.bigFileThreshold 1</code></li>
<li>Create the bundle: <code>git bundle create no_delta.bundle &lt;old&gt;..&lt;new&gt;</code>.</li>
<li>Manually remove the revisions that are ancestors of <code>&lt;old&gt;</code> using a script:</li>
</ol>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>#!/bin/bash
bundle_file=&quot;$1&quot;
old_sha=&quot;$2&quot;

prerequisites=&quot;$(strings &quot;$bundle_file&quot; | grep -o -E  '^-([0-9a-f]){40}')&quot;
ex_cmds=&quot;&quot;
while read -r prereq; do
  prereq=&quot;${prereq:1}&quot;
  if [[ &quot;$prereq&quot; = &quot;$old_sha&quot; ]]; then
   continue
  fi

  if git merge-base --is-ancestor ${prereq} ${old_sha}; then
    ex_cmds+=&quot;g/-${prereq}/d&quot;$'\n'
  else
    echo &quot;Preserve ${prereq}&quot;
  fi
done &lt;&lt;&lt;&quot;$prerequisites&quot;
ex_cmds+=$'wq'
echo &quot;${ex_cmds}&quot;
echo &quot;${ex_cmds}&quot; | ex -b &quot;$bundle_file&quot;
</code></pre>
<ol start="4">
<li>Restore delta compression: <code>git config unset core.bigFileThreshold</code></li>
</ol>
